  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Using the common logarithm and scientific notation, evaluate each of the following correct to three significant figures:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$123\\times321$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3.95\\times10^4$",
          "worked": "Using the common-logarithm table:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}(123\\times321)&=\\log_{10}1.23+\\log_{10}3.21+4\\\\\\log_{10}(123\\times321)&\\approx0.0899+0.5065+4\\\\\\log_{10}(123\\times321)&\\approx0.5964+4\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $10^{0.5964}\\approx3.95$.\n$$123\\times321\\approx3.95\\times10^4$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$307\\times212$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6.51\\times10^4$",
          "worked": "Using the common-logarithm table:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}(307\\times212)&=\\log_{10}3.07+\\log_{10}2.12+4\\\\\\log_{10}(307\\times212)&\\approx0.4871+0.3263+4\\\\\\log_{10}(307\\times212)&\\approx0.8134+4\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $10^{0.8134}\\approx6.51$.\n$$307\\times212\\approx6.51\\times10^4$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$812\\div653$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1.24$",
          "worked": "Writing both numbers in scientific notation, their powers of ten cancel.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}(812\\div653)&=\\log_{10}8.12-\\log_{10}6.53\\\\\\log_{10}(812\\div653)&\\approx0.9096-0.8149\\\\\\log_{10}(812\\div653)&\\approx0.0947\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse:\n$$812\\div653\\approx10^{0.0947}\\approx1.24$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$976\\div543$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1.80$",
          "worked": "Writing both numbers in scientific notation, their powers of ten cancel.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}(976\\div543)&=\\log_{10}9.76-\\log_{10}5.43\\\\\\log_{10}(976\\div543)&\\approx0.9894-0.7348\\\\\\log_{10}(976\\div543)&\\approx0.2546\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse:\n$$976\\div543\\approx10^{0.2546}\\approx1.80$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q5-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$456\\times789$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3.60\\times10^5$",
          "worked": "Using the common-logarithm table:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}(456\\times789)&=\\log_{10}4.56+\\log_{10}7.89+4\\\\\\log_{10}(456\\times789)&\\approx0.6590+0.8971+4\\\\\\log_{10}(456\\times789)&\\approx0.5561+5\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $10^{0.5561}\\approx3.60$.\n$$456\\times789\\approx3.60\\times10^5$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q5-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$888\\times813$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$7.22\\times10^5$",
          "worked": "Using the common-logarithm table:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}(888\\times813)&=\\log_{10}8.88+\\log_{10}8.13+4\\\\\\log_{10}(888\\times813)&\\approx0.9484+0.9101+4\\\\\\log_{10}(888\\times813)&\\approx0.8585+5\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $10^{0.8585}\\approx7.22$.\n$$888\\times813\\approx7.22\\times10^5$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q5-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$314\\div413$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.760$",
          "worked": "Writing both numbers in scientific notation, their powers of ten cancel.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}(314\\div413)&=\\log_{10}3.14-\\log_{10}4.13\\\\\\log_{10}(314\\div413)&\\approx0.4969-0.6160\\\\\\log_{10}(314\\div413)&\\approx-0.1191\\\\\\log_{10}(314\\div413)&\\approx0.8809-1\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $10^{0.8809}\\approx7.60$.\n$$314\\div413\\approx7.60\\times10^{-1}=0.760$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q5-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$545\\div656$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.831$",
          "worked": "Writing both numbers in scientific notation, their powers of ten cancel.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}(545\\div656)&=\\log_{10}5.45-\\log_{10}6.56\\\\\\log_{10}(545\\div656)&\\approx0.7364-0.8169\\\\\\log_{10}(545\\div656)&\\approx-0.0805\\\\\\log_{10}(545\\div656)&\\approx0.9195-1\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $10^{0.9195}\\approx8.31$.\n$$545\\div656\\approx8.31\\times10^{-1}=0.831$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q5-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt{398}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$19.9$",
          "worked": "Using $398=3.98\\times10^2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}\\sqrt{398}&=\\tfrac12(\\log_{10}3.98+2)\\\\\\log_{10}\\sqrt{398}&\\approx\\tfrac12(0.5999+2)\\\\\\log_{10}\\sqrt{398}&\\approx0.29995+1\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $10^{0.29995}\\approx1.99$.\n$$\\sqrt{398}\\approx1.99\\times10^1=19.9$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q5-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt{895}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$29.9$",
          "worked": "Using $895=8.95\\times10^2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{10}\\sqrt{895}&=\\tfrac12(\\log_{10}8.95+2)\\\\\\log_{10}\\sqrt{895}&\\approx\\tfrac12(0.9518+2)\\\\\\log_{10}\\sqrt{895}&\\approx0.4759+1\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the table in reverse, $10^{0.4759}\\approx2.99$.\n$$\\sqrt{895}\\approx2.99\\times10^1=29.9$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
